  "conclusions": [
   "Removing dequant saves 0.8-0.9%; cache-resident K0 reloads give no gain, so neither DQ nor HBM/L2 limits the r3 main loop.",
   "Keeping only MFMA+barriers is 4.1% (8192) / 3.3% (4096) faster than r3: the in-loop instruction overhead ceiling. Removing barriers is 8.5% slower: the 4+4 stagger sync is required.",
   "Per-WG s_memtime/s_memrealtime probes: median SCLK 1.786 GHz (8192) under load, not 1.85; main loop 4449 cycles per K block vs 4096 ideal (92.1%); 4096x4096 additionally loses 20% to 256 WGs on 80 CUs (4 rounds)."
  ],
  "note": "Ablation variants are not GEMMs; outputs were checked only for complete overwrite/zero contracts"
 },
